Syntax: smelt <item>

Smelt reduces anything made of metal to an ingot.  It does not care what the
thing is -- a key, a shield, a ring, a chunk of ore off a cave wall -- only
what it is made of.

Half the weight comes back as metal.  Three quarters comes back if you have
gone deep into advanced blacksmithing.

Every pulse of the work is counted, landed or missed, and the ratio between
them is the grade of the bar you end with: nine tenths landed makes a
flawless ingot, less than half makes a crude one.  That grade decides how
much of the item's old stats survive being forged into something new.

The stats come across.  The armor does not, and a paired item's stats are
halved, since being a pair is what doubled them.

See also: FORGE, INGOT, MINE, WEAVE
